#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# plot_range_padding

#% text
# `plot_range_padding` is an option of graphics and plots: `plot_range_padding: f` widens automatically chosen ranges by `f` times their length on each side; the default is 0.02, and `none` gives no padding.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
plot(sin(x), [x, 0, 2pi], plot_range_padding: 0.2)
#% output
#= image("plot_range_padding.files/plot_range_padding-1.png")

#% cell
plot(sin(x), [x, 0, 2pi], plot_range_padding: none)
#% output
#= image("plot_range_padding.files/plot_range_padding-2.png")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `plot_range`, `image_size`
